sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-agential-17> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Because each gain in developmental competency makes the structural genome harder for selection to evaluate, evolution increasingly optimizes the competency mechanisms themselves, a feedback ratchet for multiscale intelligence that appears in computational models and has run to different extents in planaria, salamanders and mammals.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Competency gains drive a ratchet toward ever greater multiscale competency";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Darwin's agential materials: evolutionary implications of multiscale competency in developmental biology”, Cellular and molecular life sciences : CMLS (2023), doi:10.1007/s00018-023-04790-z; section “An evolutionary intelligence ratchet”. Scope: Evolution of metazoans; computational models of evolving competent cells"
}
